"""Chapter 14 content for the RDODI build: sources, findings, taxonomy and section bodies.
The book's chapter (3rd edition, chapter 14, Excel Spreadsheets) was read on automatetheboringstuff.com on 2026-10-01 from its
published HTML page, which the WebFetch tool declined to reproduce and which was therefore fetched with curl through the session
proxy (103,056 bytes) and converted to text; its 18 practice questions and 2 practice programs were read there. The chapter's figures
(14-1 to 14-11) are images and were NOT viewed, and the book's downloadable files (example3.xlsx, censuspopdata.xlsx,
produceSales3.xlsx) were NOT opened: small stand-in workbooks were written by the scripts instead, with the values of Table 14-1 typed
in from the page. The openpyxl documentation pages (headed 3.1.3, generated 2024-05-29), the PyPI JSON record of openpyxl and the
Python documentation pages (docs.python.org, which carried the release number 3.14.8 when read) were read online on 2026-10-01.
Every behaviour of the standard library was executed under Python 3.14.4. Every behaviour of openpyxl 3.1.5 (with et_xmlfile 2.0.0;
lxml, defusedxml and pillow not installed) was executed under Python 3.14.4 by 08-tooling/sen0414_ch14_library_run_v1_0_0.py after
installing the package into a scratch folder; its printed lines are kept in 08-tooling/sen0414_ch14_library_run_output_v1_0_0.txt and
are what the findings below quote. openpyxl is not installed in the course interpreter, so the checks of this module run only the
standard-library examples. Not executed at all: Microsoft Excel, LibreOffice Calc or Office 365 (so no formula was ever calculated by a
spreadsheet application and nothing was looked at on screen), the charts as drawn, saving over a file that is open in Excel, pandas and
NumPy, the lxml and defusedxml options, the command-line form of the two practice programs (chapter 12 is not built), and the book's
downloadable spreadsheets. A claim not in this file was not made."""
